{
  "title": "Web meal plan: duplicate/missing-recipe messages are cleared as soon as they're set",
  "description": "MealPlanPage.tsx: addMealPlan sets error(mealPlanOpError(...)) at 200 and then awaits loadMealPlans() (201), which calls setError(null) at 105, so 'duplicate' and 'recipe_missing' never show. handleEdit does the same for 'gone' and 'recipe_missing' (248-249). handleDelete ignores the op result (264), so 'gone' is silent. \
Other state in the same page: error mixes week-load failures (which hide the grid, 306/310) with action results; loadRecipes (163-178) has no request tracker so overlapping picker searches can land out of order; addMealPlan has no in-flight guard; picker open/date/mealType are three signals that can disagree (guarded at 188). \
The sync cursor in utils/mealPlanWrites.ts:13 is module-level and not keyed by user. \
Want: action results kept separate from the week-load state, and a request tracker for picker searches. iOS shows op refusals through store.refusal (MealPlanView.swift:132-146); confirm it surfaces all four results and doesn't have the same clear-on-reload issue. \
Found in the 2026-11-07 implicit-state-machine audit; line numbers are as of e94669d4ca, so re-check each point before fixing.",
